  "verbalization": "Vitetrifolin D appears to have a complex relationship with the insulin receptor, as it is directly linked to the insulin receptor through two distinct pathways. The first pathway connects Vitetrifolin D to ARO, which in turn targets the insulin receptor. The second pathway links Vitetrifolin D to Proteasome subunit beta type-2, which also targets the insulin receptor. Both ARO and Proteasome subunit beta type-2 are known to be involved in cellular processes that regulate insulin signaling and receptor activity. This suggests that Vitetrifolin D may modulate insulin receptor function through these intermediate targets. The evidence supports a mechanism where Vitetrifolin D influences insulin receptor activity via ARO or Proteasome subunit beta type-2, potentially affecting insulin signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of these intermediates in the drug's mechanism of action, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
